AB  - In the age of big data epoch, network media has developed into the core field of public comment and information sharing. User engagement through commentary improve the efficiency of public discourse by accelerating the life cycle of information, exposing, disseminating and responding. However, it also causes systemic social risks, such as group polarization, truth resolution and emotional contagion. Therefore, this research investigates influence of heuristic cues of online reviews on media credibility in social media platforms and the corresponding suggestions for intervention data analysis. In this study, 208 college students were recruited to explore the impact of the quality of online reviews and repeated exposure on media credibility, as well as the mediating role of personality traits, and to explore the interaction between the quality of online reviews and repeated exposure. The results show that repeated exposure will enhance the user 's media credibility of the news : the extroverted personality user group exhibit heightened susceptibility to accepting and propagating news information. This result suggests that users should improve their digital media literacy and rationally treat online reviews ; public sector Organizational stakeholders must strategically monitor guiding role of online comments in public opinion, strengthen monitoring and management, and build an Internet big data health network public opinion ecology.
