TI  - Fusing Headline and Content with Dual-BERT and Weighted Fusion for Fake News Detection
AU  - Nguyen, Son Thanh
AU  - Huynh, Trong Thua
AU  - Le, Tuan Anh
T3  - CCIOT '25
AB  - The proliferation of fake news threatens the integrity of information and erodes public trust. We study how headlines and full article bodies contribute, separately and jointly, to fake news detection under a unified BERT framework. We fine-tune two independent encoders (headline and body), handle long bodies with a sliding-window strategy, and evaluate three settings: headline-only, content-only, and a dual-input model. At inference, we combine the two branch probabilities using a validation-tuned weighted fusion, and we also select the decision threshold on validation to ensure fair operating points. For fairness, the same validation-based thresholding is applied to all unimodal baselines. Experiments on the publicly available, class-balanced WELFake dataset show that the dual-input fusion consistently outperforms well-tuned headline-only and content-only baselines across Accuracy, macro-F1, ROC-AUC, and Average Precision. These findings highlight the complementary value of multi-source signals and provide a practical recipe for robust, deployable fake news detectors.
