TI  - Faithful Fake News Detection Based on Natural Language Explanation Generation
AU  - Yoshida, Ko
AU  - Zhang, Jianwei
T3  - NLPIR '24
AB  - In this paper, we propose a fake news detection model that generates natural language explanations and leverages these explanations for prediction. Deep learning models, particularly Large Language Models like BERT, are effective for fake news detection. However, interpreting and explaining predictions from these complex models remains challenging. Algorithms like LIME and SHAP provide numerical explanations, but these are often insufficient for users without technical knowledge. Our model generates text-based explanations, making them more user-friendly. Experimental results show our model improves binary classification accuracy and F1-score. Additionally, we demonstrate that the explanations contribute to classification, ensuring the model’s faithfulness to the generated explanations.
