AU  - Thambiayya, Sathiyaraj
T3  - AICSS '25
AB  - In the era of information explosion, social media has become an important channel for obtaining medical information, but medical opinions are spread quickly, making it difficult to discern the integrity of these opinions. In this paper, a hybrid classification model combining LSTM and transformer networks can effectively identify and filter false information to ensure public access to accurate and reliable medical content. Experimental results show that the model performs well in classification tasks on multiple standard datasets, achieving high levels of accuracy, precision, recall, and F1 scores. In particular, when dealing with opinion data related to COVID-19, the model achieves 99.9% classification accuracy. Moreover, the hybrid classification model significantly reduces computational time costs. As a whole, the method combines high efficiency and accuracy, demonstrates the important role of modern information technology in medical text classification and public opinion management, and provides strong support for the innovation of the public health management model.
