T3  - DSAI '25
AB  - This paper focuses on the implementation of optimization of artificial intelligence (AI) techniques used in enhancing teaching and digital preservation of folk music which is a part of intangible cultural heritage. The peculiarities of folk music, like the regional variety and oral transmission, pose a challenge to the traditional ways of education and safeguarding. Taking advantage of state-of-the-art computer technologies, such as deep learning and machine learning models, this study creates customized computational solutions to overcome the problem of data scarcity and cultural authenticity issue. Adopting a mixed-methods approach involving algorithm-building, data-augmentation as well as qualitative analysis by educators and learners, this research tests the effectiveness of AI in enhancing personalized learning experience and cultural fidelity. Findings show improved student engagement as well as algorithmic performance with the presence of persistent challenges including cultural bias and lack of enough training data. The paper ends with future research directions; highlighting the combination of emerging techniques in AI and immersive technologies to develop sustainable and culturally sensitive solutions to folk music education and preservation.
