AB  - Proliferation of “Fake News” and misinformation is resulting in widespread negative social fallout. Scalable Fake News classification techniques for resource poor languages like Hindi are in early stages because of a lack of datasets and lack of robust NLP libraries for these languages. In this exploratory study we curate a dataset of around 13,000 data points of true news articles, and, articles on fake news authored by media organisations which flag fake news. We then use seven ML classification models on this dataset and present the preliminary results. Our results show that concerted efforts need to be made by the research community towards dataset curation and improving the NLP models for resource poor languages in order to make scalable classification systems.
