AB  - With the rapid development of generative artificial intelligence (GenAI), it has brought convenience to the society while also exposing many data security vulnerabilities. By applying the questionnaire survey method, the cognitive and behavioral characteristics of the public in using GenAI and facing its data security risks are analyzed. The results of the study show that although the public has a high degree of awareness of the importance of data security, there is a disconnect between cognition and behavior in actual use, and all kinds of data security risks have changed from theoretical concerns to real challenges. In response to the solution of this problem, practical countermeasures from the four dimensions of government, industry, R&amp;D and users are put forward. It is hoped that through multi-party collaboration, the data security risks of GenAI can be effectively controlled and a benign interaction between technological innovation and social development can be achieved.
