TI  - Research on the Identification and Prevention Strategies of Ideological Security Risks in Primary School Chinese Language Classrooms in the Era of Artificial Intelligence
AU  - Xu, Xinhai
AU  - Liu, Xu
AU  - Hu, Yousong
AU  - Zhao, Ziqiao
T3  - AIFE '25
AB  - The deep integration of Artificial Intelligence technology is reshaping the ecology of primary school Chinese language classrooms while introducing multiple ideological security risks such as content infiltration, algorithmic bias, and technological dependence. Comprehensively informed by theories of risk governance and collaborative filtering, this paper systematically analyzes the three core challenges faced by ideological security in AI-driven classrooms: potential risks arising from implicit content penetration, value deviations induced by algorithmic recommendations, and the excessive reliance on technological tools. In response to these challenges, this study develops a comprehensive "four-in-one" system that incorporates a Four-tier Content Review and Dynamic Monitoring Mechanism, a Collaborative Prevention Mechanism based on information literacy of teachers and students, a Human-AI Collaborative Teaching Supervision Mechanism, and specific Early Warning and Emergency Response Measures. Through multi-layered and full-process closed-loop management, this framework realizes effective identification, precise warning, and coordinated management of ideological risks, thereby providing both theoretical support and practical pathways for constructing a secure, healthy, and efficient intelligent educational environment.
