AB  - In recent years, digital learning has revolutionized educational environments, replacing traditional methods of resource acquisition and course delivery with advanced, technology-driven alternatives. Once reliant on extensive physical searches through libraries, students can now access vast educational resources with ease, thanks to rapid technological advancements. This transformation, accelerated by the COVID-19 pandemic, has brought forth new platforms for online learning, collaborative tools, and interactive multimedia networks, including mobile and instant communication tools. As technology continues to reshape education, critical questions arise regarding its impact on learning effectiveness and student cognition. With diverse learning styles and varying degrees of autonomy in digital settings, the role of adaptive learning tools and artificial intelligence (AI) in shaping knowledge acquisition, retention, and transfer becomes increasingly significant. This paper explores the cognitive shifts from traditional to digital learning, examines the evolution of learning materials and learner behavior, and critically assesses whether AI has a transformative influence on how students think and learn in modern educational contexts.
