AB  - In the digital era, new media has emerged as the primary means for Internet users to access information. With the continuous advancement of artificial intelligence technology and its deep integration with the media industry, intelligent algorithms are increasingly being integrated into social life and development processes, thereby becoming a significant determinant influencing human production and livelihood. In the context of the rapid advancement of digital technology, a series of derived risks associated with the "Social Embedding" process of artificial intelligence algorithms have been overlooked by both academia and industry. The paper elaborates on the fundamental structure of embedded in the society in artificial intelligence algorithms, examining them from several perspectives. It identifies various derived risks associated with embedded in the society and proposes a novel model for embedded in the society based on the concept of building a community for social governance. Furthermore, it presents an innovative model for governing AI algorithms within this "Social Governance Community" framework to enhance algorithm governance effectiveness and address derived risks arising from their embedded in the society.
