AU  - Luo, Yiheng
AU  - Yang, Hui
AU  - Fan, Hongbin
AU  - Li, Muzi
T3  - ICCVIT '23
AB  - Fatigue driving can easily lead to traffic accidents. Therefore, fatigue driving behavior needs to be analyzed. Compared to normal driving, human facial expressions in a state of fatigue can be changed. We integrate facial expression recognition technology into the recognition of facial expressions in the state of fatigue, which can effectively determine whether a person is tired and prevent people from continuing to drive. Aiming at the problem that the accuracy rate of facial expression recognition algorithm is not high, a multi-hidden layer classification algorithm (DCNN-SVM) is proposed by combining deep convolutional neural network (DCNN) and support vector machine (SVM). We further analyze the characteristics of facial expressions under fatigue driving, and apply the algorithm to the recognition of fatigued facial expressions. In the recognition process, we select a part of the face image from the face image database CMU face image as the training data set and a part of the image from the face image database CMU as the test data set. The ratio of the training dataset to the test dataset is 4:1. During the training process, the features of fatigued facial expressions are extracted by DCNN and applied to the image classification of SVM to obtain a classifier for fatigue expressions. During testing, classifiers are placed into a test data set for testing. In the experimental process, we compare the DCNN algorithm and SVM algorithm with the proposed DCNN-SVM algorithm, change the parameters of DCNN and SVM, and analyze their influence on the recognition effect. Therefore, this paper proves the effectiveness of the proposed algorithm.
