AB  - In order to explore the impact of host country environmental risk on overseas merger and acquisition(M&amp;A) results of Chinese state-owned enterprises, this study selects 73 indicators from five risk levels: political and legal risks, economic risks, social and cultural risks, natural risks, and technological risks to construct a risk index system. Through RF-RFECV-based feature selection, 19 indicators that have the greatest impact on overseas M&amp;A results of state-owned enterprises are determined. The key risks selected through feature selection are characterized, and the state of state-owned enterprise M&amp;A events is labeled for deep learning. Through model comparison, it is found that deep neural network demonstrates significant advantages in dealing with overseas M&amp;A risk data sets of state-owned enterprises. The research results provide scientific theoretical support for overseas M&amp;A decision of state-owned enterprises, help to improve the ability of enterprises to cope with overseas environmental risks during overseas M&amp;A, and promote the steady development of Chinese state-owned enterprises in the international market.
