AB  - With the widespread adoption of AI algorithms and the transformative impact of 5G and 4K/8K technologies in media production, the training of television directing talent faces new challenges and opportunities. This study explores the potential applications of AI in practical teaching, particularly in multi-camera switching, real-time image processing, and automated editing. In parallel, the evolution of online live broadcasting, accelerated by post-pandemic media dynamics and heightened viewer expectations, necessitates a sophisticated skill set for TV directors. As crucial figures in live broadcasts, TV directors must navigate these technological advancements and the changing aesthetic landscape. This paper proposes a comprehensive, hybrid teaching model that integrates AI technologies with Electronic Studio Production (ESP) and Electronic Field Production (EFP) methods. By doing so, it aims to enhance students' practical skills, problem-solving abilities, and collaborative capabilities. Our findings highlight the importance of immersive practical training in preparing students for the evolving demands of TV directing in the context of new media.
