AB  - It is our great pleasure to welcome you to the 3rd Workshop on Recent Advances in Resilient and Trustworthy MAchine learning-driveN systems (ARTMAN), co-located with ACM CCS 2025 in Taipei. Thought as a forum to enable the gathering of several research communities from diverse domains - primarily security &amp; privacy and machine learning, but also various application fields, ARTMAN seeks to push forward the discussion and collaboration between attendees, including both researchers and practitioners. The mission of the symposium is to collectively explore and discuss the topics about resilient and trustworthy machine learning-powered applications and systems, for academic researchers to share their views, experiences, and lessons learned, as well as for industrial practitioners to provide their insights and perspectives. ARTMAN gives researchers and practitioners a unique opportunity to collaboratively close the gap between the actual industry concerns with respect to the resilience and trust of ML systems, and the abundant academic research corpus on adversarial machine learning, in particular for autonomous networks.
