TI  - Rethinking on Misleading of Machine Learning in Bank Risk Warning System
AU  - Xiao, Yan
AU  - He, Zehao
AU  - Liu, Yuyang
T3  - ICMLCA '23
AB  - Machine learning is widely used in the bank risk warning system more and more popular. It has been able to provide early internal bank risk warning nowadays. However, its ability of external risk warning is limited and need a long way to go to meet the needs of bank risk warning system. This study shows that external bank risk warning information, especially the subtle information provided by the machine learning would mislead the bank risk warning system. Analyses indicated that machine learning relied heavily on the accuracy of data, typically provided predictive rather than deterministic results, overlooked or underestimated unexpected events during the learning process, and it might provide opposite predictive results when dealing with external subtle information. With the supports of external subtle information filtering criteria and bank simulation training center, machine learning could jointly improve its ability to process external subtle information and reduce the possibilities of misleading in bank risk warning system.
