AB  - The Sybil assault is one example of a sort of attack that targets distributed systems and uses numerous identities to influence network behavior. In numerous distributed systems, including peer-to-peer networks, social networks, and blockchain networks, Sybil attacks have been used. The current paper summarizes the pertinent studies on Sybil attacks, discusses how to avoid them, and offers potential countermeasures to Sybil attacks. The solutions are divided into two groups: those relying on machine learning and those not. The study concludes by highlighting the importance of understanding how to defend against Sybil assaults and providing insightful information on the numerous aspects affecting vulnerable systems.
