AB  - In order to alleviate the information disadvantage faced by small and medium-sized investors in capital markets, the Shenzhen Stock Exchange and the Shanghai Stock Exchange introduced interactive communication platforms. The Q&amp;R data from board secretaries on these platforms contains high-density investor sentiment information. To enhance the accuracy of investor sentiment analysis, we propose an integrated deep learning approach that considers both the related news of investor questions and the questions themselves. In this paper, we employ deep learning and rule-based named entity recognition to retrospectively trace news related to investor queries. Combining this with the text of investor inquiries, we utilize the Bert deep learning model for comprehensive sentiment analysis. The proposed method achieves a sentiment analysis accuracy of 90%, demonstrating a ∼8% improvement over considering only investor questions. This innovative approach contributes to both data and methodology in the realm of board secretary Q&amp;R research, providing a reference for future studies.
