AB  - Early rumor detection has been gaining increasing attention because of tremendous effects caused by fake or unverified information. There are multiple detection methods, but the performance results are not satisfactory when they are applied to early rumor detection. This paper proposes a novel method based on deep learning. Using Transformer as a feature extraction framework, it can better recognize and understand text content. In addition, the problem of gradient vanished of long texts is solved by Bidirectional Long Short-Term Memory (BLSTM). The results of the proposed detection methodology suggest that it has excellent accuracy of 0.925 and other evaluation indicators of excessing 0.9 when using massive news derived from Weibo as a dataset for experiments. The aims of the research are expected to assist users distinguishing the fake news and prevent the rumors from spreading.
