TI  - MAD' 25: Proceedings of the 4th ACM International Workshop on Multimedia AI against Disinformation
AB  - It is our great pleasure to welcome you to the 4th ACM International Workshop on Multimedia AI against Disinformation - MAD '25. In today's interconnected digital world, sharing information with billions of people happens almost instantaneously. Social media platforms, websites, and real-time user interactions serve as powerful channels for spreading news and ideas. Unfortunately, this rapid exchange has also fueled a sharp rise in misinformation, disinformation, and propaganda. As the volume of deceptive content grows daily, protecting the integrity of public discourse has become more critical than ever.The rise of AI-driven content generation has introduced a new layer of complexity. With AI capable of producing and altering images, videos, audio, and text, distinguishing between real and manipulated content is increasingly difficult. This has raised serious concerns about the credibility of digital media. To address this, there is a growing need for AI-powered tools that can reliably detect and identify synthetic or tampered content, supporting journalists, researchers, and fact-checkers in their efforts to combat the spread of false information.Looking ahead, the fight against disinformation will depend on advanced AI techniques that can handle multiple types of media simultaneously. Now in its fourth edition, the workshop aims to serve as a platform for sharing innovations and research focused on AI-based disinformation detection, content verification, and mitigation strategies.
