AB  - To enhance the efficiency and interpretability of news classification, this study proposes a CART decision tree-based news classification method. This paper elaborates on the construction steps of decision tree recursive partitioning using the CART algorithm. We use CountVectorizer to extract features from the ISOT Fake News Dataset and validate the model performance via comparative experiments. The novelty of this study, as compared with existing research, lies in verifying the applicability of CART decision trees in the scenario of fake news classification. The experimental results show that the model achieves an accuracy of 94.4% and a precision of 95.0% on the test set, both outperforming the Bayesian classification model. This confirms that CART decision trees can be effectively applied to news classification tasks.
