TY  - CONF
TI  - Adaptive Both homo- and hetero-Feature Integration for Multimodal Emotion Recognition
AU  - Wang, Ze Kun
AU  - Si, Zhan Jun
T3  - MMAsia '24
AB  - In Multimodal Emotion Recognition (MER), learning to represent and fuse modalities while handling long multimodal sequences is crucial. Existing studies typically encode multimodal content as deterministic points in a semantic subspace and fuse these multimodal features through simple concatenation or attention mechanisms. However, most approaches struggle with noisy multimodal content and the challenges posed by long sequences. To address these issues, we propose a novel approach for multimodal heterogeneity adaptation, with two key modules: the Integrating Mamba Sequence (IMS) for homogeneous features and the Uncertainty Consistent Fusion (UCF) for heterogeneous features. The IMS module treats homogeneous features as primary events, using a residual feature extractor to reduce noise and Mamba as the backbone to enhance long-sequence modeling. The UCF module first combines complementary information from different modalities, then quantifies inter-modality uncertainty, and learns the underlying distribution of each modality by constraining variance, thereby adaptively fusing multimodal features. Ultimately, the fused homogeneous and heterogeneous features are used for human emotion prediction. Experimental results on multiple human emotion recognition benchmarks clearly demonstrate the superiority of our model.
