AB  - It is our great pleasure to welcome you to the 1st Deepfake Forensics Workshop: Detection, Attribution, Recognition, and Adversarial Challenges in the Era of AI-Generated Media - DFF-2025 at ACM MM 2025. This workshop aims to build a specialized community dedicated to addressing the forensic challenges posed by AI-generated content. In recent years, Deepfake technologies have seen unprecedented advances, becoming a central issue in multimedia analysis and raising urgent questions about authenticity and reliability.The purpose of DFF-2025 is not only to present methods addressing current challenges in Deepfake detection, but also to promote the exchange of ideas, solutions, and forward-looking perspectives that can drive future advances in Deepfake attribution, recognition, and adversarial forensics. Given the fast evolution of generative models, we are aware that approaches effective today may quickly lose relevance. For this reason, it is essential to promote an interdisciplinary community in which researchers actively share and discuss innovative strategies, linking multimedia forensics, adversarial machine learning, and legalethical perspectives. Through this dialogue, the workshop seeks to advance robust and generalizable methodologies, strengthening the role of deepfake forensics in safeguarding the integrity and trustworthiness of digital content.
